# 🧭 1. The Big Picture

A bug bounty workflow is more than finding a payload that works. You need to understand the target, identify a real security issue, prove it safely, explain its impact, and help the organization fix it.

```text
       AUTHORIZED TARGET
              │
              ▼
       ① SCOPE DISCOVERY
              │
              ▼
       ② RECONNAISSANCE
       ├── Domains & subdomains
       ├── Ports & services
       ├── Directories & files
       ├── OSINT & exposed data
       └── Technology fingerprinting
              │
              ▼
       ③ TESTING
       ├── Find input points
       ├── Test how input is handled
       └── Validate a security impact
              │
              ▼
       ④ EVIDENCE + REPRODUCTION
              │
              ▼
       ⑤ PROFESSIONAL REPORT
              │
              ▼
       TRIAGE → FIX → RESOLUTION
```

**Learning rule:** Understand what each tool does before automating it. The source material recommends beginning with manual reconnaissance so you learn the process and can build a workflow that makes sense.

